                <pb facs="0320" n="289" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v02/pg289"/>

                <head>134. Memorandum From the Executive Secretary of the Department of State
                    (Eliot) to the Assistant Secretary of State for European Affairs
                        (Hillenbrand)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d134-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1971-01-18">January 18, 1971</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Coordination of Official Contacts with the USSR </item>
                </list>
                <p>Upon reading Mr. Kissinger’s memorandum of January 7 on the above subject,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d134-f2"/> the Secretary asked me to inform you that the
                    procedures outlined in the memorandum should not alter our internal procedures
                    for clearances of substantive cables with the White House. This means that such
                    cables will only be cleared with the White House if the Secretary, the Under
                    Secretary, or the Under Secretary for Political Affairs deem it necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed> Theodore L. Eliot Jr.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d134-f3"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
